{"page":151,"blocks":[{"x":0.7305,"y":0.05257,"w":0.22101,"h":0.01535,"fs":0.01535,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"3.3 Differentiation Rules 137"},{"x":0.39285,"y":0.10752,"w":0.26484,"h":0.03283,"fs":0.01279,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"Derivative of a Positive Integer Power If n is a positive integer, then"},{"x":0.60928,"y":0.15014,"w":0.09563,"h":0.02727,"fs":0.01279,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"d dxxn = nxn-1."},{"x":0.36258,"y":0.2097,"w":0.40524,"h":0.01391,"fs":0.01311,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"Proof of the Positive Integer Power Rule The formula"},{"x":0.09953,"y":0.22018,"w":0.1615,"h":0.01023,"fs":0.01023,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"HISTORICAL BIOGRAPHY"},{"x":0.46374,"y":0.22868,"w":0.38673,"h":0.01853,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":0,"t":"zn - xn = (z - x)(zn-1 + zn-2 x + g + zxn-2 + xn-1)"},{"x":0.09953,"y":0.23565,"w":0.10148,"h":0.02365,"fs":0.01023,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"Richard Courant (1888–1972)"},{"x":0.36259,"y":0.25685,"w":0.59302,"h":0.02814,"fs":0.01279,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"can be verified by multiplying out the right-hand side. Then from the alternative formula for the definition of the derivative,"},{"x":0.67277,"y":0.28874,"w":0.04965,"h":0.01793,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"zn - xn"},{"x":0.5474,"y":0.29183,"w":0.07607,"h":0.01347,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"ƒ(z) - ƒ(x)"},{"x":0.46647,"y":0.30132,"w":0.07825,"h":0.01347,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"ƒ′(x) = lim"},{"x":0.56645,"y":0.30132,"w":0.10362,"h":0.01771,"fs":0.01279,"n":2,"k":0,"t":"z - x = lim"},{"x":0.67855,"y":0.30558,"w":0.038,"h":0.01346,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"z - x"},{"x":0.52254,"y":0.31174,"w":0.02264,"h":0.01038,"fs":0.00895,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"zSx"},{"x":0.64791,"y":0.31174,"w":0.02264,"h":0.01038,"fs":0.00895,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"zSx"},{"x":0.52254,"y":0.32536,"w":0.35409,"h":0.02528,"fs":0.01279,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"zSx(zn-1 + zn-2x + g + zxn-2 + xn-1) n terms"},{"x":0.50555,"y":0.32984,"w":0.03916,"h":0.01347,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"= lim"},{"x":0.50555,"y":0.35677,"w":0.05752,"h":0.01467,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"= nxn-1."},{"x":0.36258,"y":0.38805,"w":0.59303,"h":0.05885,"fs":0.01279,"n":4,"k":1,"t":"The Power Rule is actually valid for all real numbers n. We have seen examples for a negative integer and fractional power, but n could be an irrational number as well. To apply the Power Rule, we subtract 1 from the original exponent n and multiply the result by n. Here we state the general version of the rule, but postpone its proof until Section 3.8."},{"x":0.39285,"y":0.47918,"w":0.1869,"h":0.03051,"fs":0.01279,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"Power Rule (General Version) If n is any real number, then"},{"x":0.60928,"y":0.51949,"w":0.09563,"h":0.02727,"fs":0.01279,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"d dxxn = nxn-1,"},{"x":0.39284,"y":0.55551,"w":0.33237,"h":0.01467,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"for all x where the powers xn and xn-1 are defined."},{"x":0.36258,"y":0.61918,"w":0.38036,"h":0.01449,"fs":0.01407,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"EXAMPLE 1 Differentiate the following powers of x."},{"x":0.63906,"y":0.64216,"w":0.21136,"h":0.03019,"fs":0.01279,"n":3,"k":0,"t":"x4 (e) x-4>3 (f) 2x2+p"},{"x":0.36258,"y":0.64365,"w":0.28717,"h":0.01982,"fs":0.01279,"n":4,"k":0,"t":"(a) x3 (b) x2/3 (c) x22 (d) 1"},{"x":0.36258,"y":0.67668,"w":0.05909,"h":0.01279,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"Solution"},{"x":0.36258,"y":0.69629,"w":0.18415,"h":0.0276,"fs":0.01401,"n":3,"k":1,"t":"(a) d dx (x3) = 3x3-1 = 3x2"},{"x":0.09757,"y":0.70361,"w":0.24807,"h":0.04094,"fs":0.01151,"n":3,"k":1,"t":"Applying the Power Rule Subtract 1 from the exponent and multiply the result by the original exponent."},{"x":0.36258,"y":0.72926,"w":0.12063,"h":0.02891,"fs":0.01401,"n":3,"k":0,"t":"(b) d dx (x2>3) = 2"},{"x":0.47503,"y":0.72926,"w":0.11929,"h":0.02843,"fs":0.01279,"n":2,"k":0,"t":"3x(2>3)-1 = 2 3x-1>3"},{"x":0.36258,"y":0.75621,"w":0.17849,"h":0.0359,"fs":0.01441,"n":3,"k":0,"t":"(c) d dx 1x222 = 22x22-1"},{"x":0.36258,"y":0.79588,"w":0.07077,"h":0.0305,"fs":0.01279,"n":3,"k":0,"t":"(d) d dx a 1"},{"x":0.42266,"y":0.79588,"w":0.06002,"h":0.03211,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"x4b = d"},{"x":0.47088,"y":0.79929,"w":0.24559,"h":0.02742,"fs":0.01401,"n":1,"k":0,"t":"dx (x-4) = -4x-4-1 = -4x-5 = - 4"},{"x":0.70578,"y":0.81388,"w":0.0132,"h":0.01419,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"x5"},{"x":0.36258,"y":0.834,"w":0.14133,"h":0.02891,"fs":0.01401,"n":3,"k":0,"t":"(e) d dx (x-4>3) = - 4"},{"x":0.49573,"y":0.834,"w":0.13958,"h":0.02843,"fs":0.01279,"n":2,"k":0,"t":"3x-(4>3)-1 = - 4 3x-7>3"},{"x":0.36258,"y":0.86159,"w":0.1494,"h":0.0359,"fs":0.01441,"n":3,"k":0,"t":"(f) d dx 1 2x2+p2 = d"},{"x":0.50019,"y":0.86159,"w":0.16231,"h":0.0359,"fs":0.01441,"n":1,"k":0,"t":"dx 1x1+(p>2)2 = a1 + p"},{"x":0.65267,"y":0.86699,"w":0.20998,"h":0.03044,"fs":0.01279,"n":2,"k":0,"t":"2 b x1+(p>2)-1 = 1 2 (2 + p)2xp"},{"x":0.36258,"y":0.90749,"w":0.59297,"h":0.02814,"fs":0.01279,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"The next rule says that when a differentiable function is multiplied by a constant, its derivative is multiplied by the same constant."}]}